Package: toxplot
Type: Package
Title: Batch Processing, Modeling and Visualizing the Dose-Response of High-Throughput Screening Bioassay
Version: 0.1.2
Authors@R: person("Jun", "Wang", email = "njekin@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Batch processing of high-throughput toxicology bioassay screening
    data from a primary inhibition assay and a companion cytotoxicity assay.
    Provides data normalization, quality-control analysis, dose-response curve
    fitting using the Hill model in 'tcpl', visualization, and toxicity-adjusted
    potency ranking. Curve fitting uses the ToxCast pipeline described by
    Filer et al. (2017) <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btw680>. The toxicity-adjusted
    ranking method is described by Wang et al. (2018)
    <doi:10.1021/acs.est.7b06145>.
URL: https://github.com/njekin/ToxPlot-R-Package
BugReports: https://github.com/njekin/ToxPlot-R-Package/issues
License: GPL (>= 2)
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
Depends: R (>= 3.3.0)
Imports:
    dplyr (>= 0.5.0),
    tcpl (>= 1.0.0),
    ggplot2 (>= 3.4.0),
    ggthemes (>= 3.4.0)
Suggests: knitr,
    rmarkdown,
